          "type": "data",
          "data": {
            "text/markdown": "<span class=\"markdown prose dark:prose-invert contents\"><h2 id=\"a-squared-tadpole-epsilon-terms-change-the-finite-answer\">A squared tadpole: epsilon terms change the finite answer</h2>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">For <marimo-tex class=\"arithmatex\">||(I_2=\\int_k (k^2-m^2+i0)^{-2}||)</marimo-tex>, reduction gives\n<marimo-tex class=\"arithmatex\">||(I_2=(d-2)A_0(m^2;\\mu^2)/(2m^2)||)</marimo-tex>.\nSince <marimo-tex class=\"arithmatex\">||((d-2)/(2m^2)=(1-\\epsilon)/m^2||)</marimo-tex>, the tadpole's pole contributes\nan additional <marimo-tex class=\"arithmatex\">||(-1||)</marimo-tex> to the finite term. Setting <marimo-tex class=\"arithmatex\">||(d=4||)</marimo-tex> prematurely would\nmiss it. The correct coefficients are\n<marimo-tex class=\"arithmatex\">||([-\\log(m^2/\\mu^2),\\,1,\\,0]||)</marimo-tex>.</span></span>"
          }
        }
      ],
      "console": []
